    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Lexicon is a brand naming studio founded in 1982 by David Placek in Sausalito, CA. ~29 employees. Responsible for some of the most recognizable product names in history: Pentium (Intel), PowerBook (Apple), BlackBerry, Swiffer and Febreze (P&G), Dasani (Coca-Cola), Azure (Microsoft), Sonos, Impossible Foods, Vercel. Process combines structural linguistics, a global network of 100+ linguists across 75 countries, consumer research, and trademark clearance -- highly specialized, deeply expert, not a generalist agency. Senior/founder-led studio; David Placek has run it for 40+ years. Autonomy: N/A (org entry). Jonathan's note: \"the goats of naming.\"",
      "source_url": null,
